WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.310
Look. Something like this? What do you think?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.920
Yes. A little bit more this way, here.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.450
It looks lovely.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.660
Miya-sama!

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.390
You two have improved a lot.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.210
Thank you very much! <i> </i>

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.690
Thank you very much! Thank you very much!

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.400
Do you have any plans for this coming weekend?

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.070
Well I... <i> </i>

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:18.740
Well I... No! No plans!

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.820
No! No plans!

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:21.800
Nothing!

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.610
Really? Thank goodness.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.200
This coming weekend,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.550
...the senior members and I are going to my vacation home.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.080
We will plan and prepare for my birthday party.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.690
I've been looking forward to your birthday!

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:42.360
Thank you, Shinobu-san.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.560
You're welcome.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:49.770
There are... some things for the party you could help me prepare.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.040
Can you two come with us?

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.900
Yes! Gladly!

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.380
Here, have some juice, Nanako-san.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.850
I don't want it.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.250
You're still upset?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.250
Of course!

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:10.990
Mariko-san! Wait!

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.270
We made a promise to Tomoko.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.930
We said we'd all go somewhere together.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.460
It can't be helped! That was a request from Miya-sama.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.800
Besides, we've already been given two round-trip tickets.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.600
It was YOU who promised Miya-sama!

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.940
I don't know anything about it! I'll go somewhere with Tomoko.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.750
That promise to Tomoko-san was only in case nothing else happened.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:35.950
So that settles that.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.150
You're mean!

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.150
Anyway, we're already on the train.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.490
I've already given her such a hard time! Poor Tomoko. Darn.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.690
I see.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:49.560
I'm sorry! Miya-sama asked us.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.600
I see.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.430
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.630
How can you just say "Sorry!"...?

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.500
Founder's Day is coming!

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.770
And I have to spend it alone?

00:03:58.900 --> 00:03:59.500
But..!

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.710
You should see all this!!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.040
...just as I promised - guidebooks, scheduling, pricing.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.650
I'd taken care of all of it!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:09.780
A souvenir, then! <i> </i>

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.510
A souvenir, then! What?

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.770
A souvenir! Whether I ever speak to you again,

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.190
...depends upon the souvenir you bring me.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.660
So of course, I'll pay for the souvenir.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.060
That's not the point.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.460
I'm sorry.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:26.600
Geez.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.490
I'm hungry!

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.420
Please...

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.080
As you can guess, my dear Brother,

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:59.500
...we are on our way to Miya-sama's vacation home!

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:05.520
<b>22. A Summer's Serenade</b>

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.150
Welcome, Milady.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.590
It's a pleasure to have you here.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.790
We'll have two more joining us. Please see to their needs.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:29.930
Certainly, Ma'am.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.800
Now! Take the luggage out of the car.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.100
OK.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.140
Minako-san!

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.070
Oh! That's right!

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.540
Yes, right away!

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.610
Sorry, can you take this...?

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.880
I'm terribly sorry about that.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.220
You're hopeless, forgetting such a thing...

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.890
It slipped my mind... I was so...

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.290
Here it is.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.430
Please see to our guests.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:06.300
I'll be spending my time alone.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:09.170
I will. Certainly.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.260
That summer's day.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:04.360
That summer's day.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.490
That summer's day is still here.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.040
Minako-san!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.000
Minako-san!

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.840
I... Yes?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.840
You made another mistake!

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:29.980
This time, you got the watch and the pencil case reversed!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.450
I'm sorry.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.120
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.590
Every single detail in that room must remain unchanged!

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.330
I'm terribly sorry. I'll put them...

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.330
Never mind.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.200
I've already corrected them.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:52.610
Oh... it's wonderful! It's like a Chateau on the Rhine River!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.470
Welcome. This way please.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.750
You're so kind to think of us.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:07.690
First year members have never been invited here before.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.690
You should feel very honored.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:10.690
Yes! <i> </i>

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.100
Yes! Y...yes!

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.890
Where is Miya-sama?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.360
Taking a walk. You can see her later.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:18.430
OK!

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.970
So now, perhaps I should show you what we have for you.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.440
OK!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.580
This sun room will be your work room.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.580
My Brother...

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.320
Our assignment was to prepare all the invitations

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.930
...for Miya-sama birthday party the following week.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:51.400
There were about 300 names, filling two address books.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.470
I ever wondered if it could be finished in a single weekend!

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:59.870
A trip with Tomoko might have been better, after all.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:05.410
Wow! How beautiful!

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.550
Mariko-san, look! The lake is shimmering!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.020
We can't stop now.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.560
Let's go for a walk!

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.160
We should after coming all the way here!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:17.560
I'll pass...

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.530
A violin?

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:38.310
Softly...

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:43.040
Like a melancholy cry for help,

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:47.380
...the music gently penetrated the deep woods.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.250
For whom was she crying out?

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.010
Fukiko-sama, proud Fukiko-sama...

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:58.260
...crying for help, but to whom?

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:04.470
As if suffering the unbearable pain of tragic love...

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:06.930
...love?

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.400
Her love?

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:16.610
But... who?

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.560
Perhaps it was the coffee I had with dinner...

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:34.430
Though Mariko-san was sleeping soundly,

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:38.700
...somehow tonight I was unable to fall asleep.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:44.040
It must've been past one o'clock.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.850
I heard a splash of water nearby.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.950
That summer's day.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.390
That was definitely Miya-sama.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:24.470
The trail of droplets led upward,

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.540
...past Miya-sama's bedroom.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:32.400
At the end of a long hallway, after a couple of turns,

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:36.490
...I heard her voice again from behind the door.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:39.820
That summer's day.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.690
Shall I compare thee to a summer's day?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:48.980
No, Thou art more lovely and more temperate.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:53.840
Rough winds do shake the darling buds of May,

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:57.170
And summer's lease hath all too short a date.

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:02.880
Sometime hot the eye of heaven shines, oft his gold complexion dims,

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:07.980
Fair from fair sometime declines, by nature's changing course.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:14.310
But thy eternal summer shall not fade,

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:17.700
Nor shall Death brag,

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.530
..thou wanderest in his Shade.

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:22.930
When in eternal lines to time thou growest.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.540
In eternal lines to time thou growest!

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.880
Who's there!?

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:37.210
What's going on?! Where've you been?

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:40.880
Umm...well... the bathroom. The downstairs one.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.880
What a shock! Waking up and finding myself alone in bed here...!

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.280
I'm sorry!

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:49.420
Don't leave me alone again!

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:50.690
Alright, I won't.

00:16:09.770 --> 00:16:12.440
Would you care for more coffee?

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:16.180
No, I'm fine. Thank you.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:22.590
Her smile is elegant, quiet, and calm.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:29.590
As if nothing at all had happened last night.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:33.600
Miya-sama appears no different today.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:37.030
But that voice remains with me.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:39.240
Her voice from that room.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:43.610
...a voice which seemed torn from her deepest heart.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:08.030
Oh... they're so pretentious. Playing badminton.

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:10.370
The last train is at 8, tonight.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.500
If we don't finish, we'll have to take it home with us.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.570
Nanako-san, how many do you have left?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.040
Umm... about 50.

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:22.710
Wow... you're lucky! I have at least 120!

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.720
I've brought something cool to drink.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:28.050
Oh! Thank you!

00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:30.120
It's hard work, huh?

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.660
Thank you, very much.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:46.000
Excuse me...

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:48.410
Something I can do for you?

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:54.480
Whose room is that, on the 3rd floor, at the very end of the hallway?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:57.280
Oh, the "sealed chamber".

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.620
The "sealed chamber"?

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.890
Yes, that's what we call it.

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:08.830
That room was Fukiki-sama's, until she turned 12.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:12.160
It's been left exactly as it was then.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.300
As it was? Why?

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:15.700
Minako-san.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:23.980
Speaking about family matters to our guests is forbidden.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.510
I... I sincerely apologize.

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.780
Get out of my sight.

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:29.910
Yes ma'am.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:41.130
Igarasi-san! Igarasi-san, are you there?

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:43.260
Yes, Milady.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.200
Fire her.

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:49.130
Please get rid of Minako-san immediately!

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.340
What!

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.410
What did she do?

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:57.410
She's not suitable to serve the Ichinomiya family as a maid.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:59.480
Isn't that reason enough?

00:18:59.810 --> 00:19:01.150
But can't you...

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.080
Those are my orders.

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:05.420
Very well, I'll do it.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:13.290
But... but I only asked her about the room!

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:17.230
Miya-sama! Please wait, Miya-sama!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:22.400
It was me! I asked her about that room. It's not her fault!

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:22.430
Don't be concerned. No need to defend her.
It was me! I asked her about that room. It's not her fault!

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.370
Don't be concerned. No need to defend her.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.510
That wasn't entirely over what happened today.

00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:28.570
But...

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:31.840
You aren't involved in this. Understood?

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:44.320
Wait!

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.870
I'm really sorry. It was all my fault.

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:02.940
It's OK. I'm a born gossip.

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:05.950
But to be fired so suddenly...!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:07.810
No need for worry.

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:12.080
I just wanted to see what being a maid was like.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:16.490
It's like my hobby, to change jobs!

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:21.430
Thanks, but I'll be fine.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:24.230
I'm living with my parents in a neighboring town.

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:25.030
Really? <i> </i>

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.030
Really? Yes.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.900
You're as kind as you look.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.770
What?

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:34.040
Kind people draw me out like that -- I can't help it.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.510
About the "sealed chamber"...

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:38.400
Yes?

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:41.780
No one can go inside except Fukiko-sama.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:42.850
No one?

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:44.720
Not even other family members.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.990
On the day before Fukiko-sama arrived,

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:51.190
I was sent in to clean the room.

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:53.790
What a strange room.

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:57.130
Fukiko-sama would scold me mercilessly,

00:20:57.130 --> 00:21:01.130
...if there was even the slightest change in a doll's location!

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:03.800
Everything is exactly as it was 6 years ago?

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:07.340
When Miya-sama was 12 years old?

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.880
Bye. Take care!

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:11.540
You, too.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:37.570
Nanako-san, this lake is very dear to me.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:45.110
Miya-sama!

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:50.320
Miya-sama!

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:51.900
Miya-sama!

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:05.000
Come on in, Nanako-san. It feels so good!

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.000
What? But...

00:22:57.250 --> 00:23:00.450
I'm sorry, Nanako-san. I'm truly sorry.

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:03.590
I just wanted you to swim with me.

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:05.730
Are you okay, Nanako-san?

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:08.260
I'm fine.

00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:09.600
I'm sorry.

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:18.140
Say, Nanako-san, are you really okay?

00:23:18.270 --> 00:23:20.610
I heard you fell in a swimming pool, and swallowed some water.

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:23.080
Sure, I'm fine now. Fine.

00:23:24.150 --> 00:23:25.710
Then, could you help me out? <i> </i>

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:26.280
Then, could you help me out? What?

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:27.020
Could you tale 50 of mine? What?

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.030
Could you tale 50 of mine? <i> </i>

00:23:30.150 --> 00:23:31.750
NO WAY!

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:37.690
My Dear Brother...

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:42.430
I may not be able to write you for a while.

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:46.900
I can't share today's experiences with anyone.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:49.240
Never, as long as I live.

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:01.300 --> 00:25:03.710
PREVIEW

00:25:03.710 --> 00:25:06.650
At her 18th birthday party,

00:25:06.650 --> 00:25:11.190
Saint-Juste plays the violin in Fukiko's honor,

00:25:11.190 --> 00:25:13.320
...attempting to please her.

00:25:13.660 --> 00:25:17.060
But all of Saint-Juste's efforts come to naught,

00:25:17.060 --> 00:25:19.330
when Fukiko reacts unexpectedly...

00:25:19.800 --> 00:25:20.840
Next episode: <i> </i>

00:25:20.840 --> 00:25:22.780
Next episode: The Forbidden Gift

00:25:23.130 --> 00:25:24.700
Brother, Dear Brother... <i> </i>

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:27.540
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
